From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:37:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/46] phy: qcom: qmp-pcie: Add SM8475 gen3x1 PCIe PHY

SM8475 PCIe0 is the V6 gen3x2 PHY found on SAR2130P/SM8550, used with one
lane and lane 1 held off through its PCS. The vendor qcom,phy-sequence
matches the SAR2130P serdes table except LOCK_CMP1_MODE0 (0x0a), the
SM8550 RX table except TX_ADAPT_POST_THRESH (0xf0), the SM8550 PCS table,
and only the power state/refclk part of the SM8550 PCS misc table.
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c | 112 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 112 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c
index 3618812e8..16a616e01 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c
@@ -3129,6 +3129,86 @@ static const struct qmp_phy_init_tbl sar2130p_qmp_gen3x2_pcie_rc_serdes_tbl[] =
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(QSERDES_V6_COM_CORE_CLK_EN, 0xa0),
 };
 
